ngth to your teammate and suggest they continue leading, but with 8 cards left, they may not have coordination. Also, passing gives the landlord free rein — they might start a new lead that could be dangerous.\n\nThus, playing a minimal card like ♣6 is a safe way to continue the sequence without overcommitting.\n\nReason: Playing ♣6 beats the previous ♦5 with the smallest possible upgrade, potentially forcing the landlord to use a higher card. Since the landlord is down to 2 cards, every forced play increases the chance they waste an important card or get stuck. It also avoids clogging your hand with low-value singles you can\'t use later. Passing risks giving up control completely.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣6"]}'}
